*   convex.sno - the public entry point for the native SNOBOL4 Convex
*   client. Include this one file to get HTTPS query/mutation/action and
*   Live sync; it exists only to give a reader and a build one obvious
*   place to start, and pulls in the layers underneath it in dependency
*   order:
*     convex-io.sno     the loaded C transport shim and its blocking helpers
*     convex-bits.sno    32-bit arithmetic for SHA-1 and WebSocket masking
*     convex-sha1.sno    SHA-1, for the WebSocket handshake only
*     convex-base64.sno  base64, for the WebSocket handshake only
*     convex-json.sno    a span-based JSON reader and a JSON writer
*     convex-error.sno   the shared cvx.err.* failure record
*     convex-http.sno    cvx.configure / cvx.query / cvx.mutation / cvx.action
*     convex-ws.sno      RFC 6455 handshake and framing
*     convex-live.sno    the pinned Convex sync protocol and reconnect logic
*
*   Public surface once this file is included:
*     cvx.configure(url, token)        set up the deployment and bearer token
*     cvx.set_auth(token)              replace the bearer token
*     cvx.query/mutation/action(path, argsraw)   one HTTP call
*     cvx.live.init()                  reset Live state for a fresh client
*     cvx.live.subscribe(path, argsraw) -> queryId
*     cvx.live.unsubscribe(queryId)
*     cvx.live.pump(deadlinems)        make one step of Live progress
*     cvx.live.next_event()            drain one queued Live update
*     cvx.live.debug_disconnect()      adapter-only forced reconnect
*     cvx.live.close()                 stop reconnecting and drop the socket
-include 'convex-live.sno'
